// Store Admin — Firestore Security Rules (no-functions build, contract 2026-11-26).
//
// RULES-LANGUAGE NOTE (coordinator fix 2026-11-26): the Firestore
// rules language has NO `if` STATEMENTS inside functions — only
// `let` bindings + a single `return` expression (ternary `? :` and
// `&&` / `||` chains do the branching). An `if` inside a function
// is a COMPILE error ("Unexpected 'if'") and the whole deploy
// fails. The Phase 2 file used `if` statements throughout and
// never compiled — it was never deployed, so nobody caught it until
// this deploy. Do NOT reintroduce `if` inside a function; every
// helper below is written as a pure expression for this reason.
// (`allow ... : if ...` on a match line is fine — that `if` is
// part of the allow syntax, not a statement.)
//
// NO Cloud Functions are deployed (Spark, no Blaze). The storefront,
// Flutter admin and Electron Store Manager write Firestore DIRECTLY
// from the client, and these rules are the trusted enforcement:
//   - Orders are created by ONE client transaction (placeOrderTx /
//     the manual-order transaction): idempotency read, product +
//     inventory reads, total from DATABASE prices, stock
//     reservation, order + movements + audit entry.
//     The order rule below re-checks the shape, every line price
//     against the products doc, and the audit
//     entry (via getAfter) — so a forged price/total is denied.
//   - Stock is reserved by the transaction (inventory.reserved +=
//     qty, absolute set). The inventory rule enforces reserved <=
//     stock on the data itself, so an over-reservation is denied and
//     the client re-reads availability.
//   - products.inStock is a DISPLAY cache refreshed by a SECOND,
//     best-effort batched write (contract §13) that sets ONLY
//     inStock, verified against the inventory doc. It is NOT updated
//     inside the order transaction (budget — see below).
//   - Feedback is a one-way card: anonymous create with the exact
//     5-field shape, no update, admin delete (spam).
//
// ANONYMOUS READS (required by the client transaction — the reads
// inside a transaction are rule-checked like any read):
//   - inventory: anonymous get (never list). The
//     transaction must read inventory (available = stock - reserved)
//     to compute availability. This
//     exposes stock counts to anyone who knows
//     a product id — the contract §3 note "stock counts stay
//     hidden" does NOT hold for the transaction reads; only the list
//     is hidden.
//   - orders: anonymous get ONLY when the doc does not exist yet
//     (resource == null) — the idempotency probe. An existing order
//     (name/phone/address) stays unreadable anonymously. Consequence:
//     a retry AFTER a successful commit (response lost) is denied at
//     the probe instead of returning the existing order; retries
//     after a failed attempt still work (the doc still does not
//     exist). Order ids are client UUIDs, not enumerable (no list).
//
// HOW THE AUDIT ENFORCEMENT WORKS (admin writes — unchanged)
// - Every admin mutation is a batched write (or a client transaction)
//   that includes its audit entry: /audit/{operationId}, where
//   operationId is a fresh UUID the app generates per operation.
// - The changed document(s) carry the same operationId as a metadata
//   field (stamped by the app alongside updatedAt), so the rule can
//   find the audit entry: getAfter(audit/{operationId}).
// - The audit entry carries a `docIds` index map:
//     docIds: { '<collection>/<docId>': [changedFields...] }
//   The rule checks that the audit entry exists in this batch, its
//   actor == request.auth.uid, its timestamp == request.time, and its
//   docIds entry for this document COVERS every field this write
//   actually changed (affectedKeys). Coverage (not exact equality):
//   the app writes full documents, so a save may list fields whose
//   values did not change — the attack the rule must stop is an
//   OMISSION (a changed field missing from the audit), and coverage
//   denies exactly that (T20). A reused operationId fails the
//   timestamp check, and the audit create fails because the document
//   already exists (T20).
// - The audit entry also carries a `newValuesByDoc` map (same keys as
//   docIds): { '<collection>/<docId>': {field: newValue...} }. The
//   rule checks that every CHANGED SENSITIVE field (price, stock,
//   reserved, status, paymentStatus, inStock, percent) is recorded
//   there with the value actually written (T20: a fake audit that
//   lists the field but records a wrong new value is denied). A flat
//   newValues map cannot hold two different values for the same field
//   when one operation touches several documents, so the per-doc map
//   is the checkable one; the flat `newValues` stays as the human
//   summary of the operation's main values.
// - Deletes carry no resource data, so the rule cannot read an
//   operationId from the write. Delete audit entries use the
//   deterministic id `del_<collection>_<docId>`; the timestamp check
//   prevents reusing a stale entry, and a second delete of the same
//   doc id fails the audit create (safe failure — auto-ids make
//   re-creation with the same id effectively impossible).
// - The `operationId`/`updatedAt` metadata fields are ignored by
//   readers (the storefront reads only its contract fields).
//
// ACCESS-CALL BUDGET: 10 calls per OPERATION, 20 per multi-doc
// request (transaction / batch) — the 10-limit applies to EACH
// operation inside a multi-doc request, not just to the request
// total (Firebase docs, "Access call limits"). That binds the order
// create, and the contract's budget math (13 <= 20) only counted the
// request total — it does NOT hold per operation. Pricing (Phase A,
// 2026-11-27) accounting per order create (platform limit 10 gets
// per operation):
//   storefront (anonymous): N product gets + 1 audit getAfter
//     + 1 fee get
//     → caps 8 lines (8 + 1 + 1 = 10). The client cap is 7 lines,
//     so no real storefront order is affected.
//   manual (authenticated admin/manager): N product gets + 1 audit
//     getAfter + 1 admins get, NO fee get — the fee
//     is client-asserted on the manual path (decision D2 keeps the
//     split) → caps 8 lines, so a 7-line manual
//     order passes at 9 gets.
//   A 9-line storefront order costs 11 gets
//   (9 + 1 + 1) and is denied by the platform limit — the
//   documented cap, not a bug. Old-shape orders (no
//   saleSavings/deliveryFee/amountDue) pay no fee get on either
//   path. No check was
//   weakened to fit — this is reported, not silently worked around.
//   Every other operation in the transaction costs 0-1 calls:
//     inventory reservation 0, movements 0, audit (anonymous) 0,
//     audit (admin) 1 cached admins get.
//   The §13 inStock refresh is a separate batch: 1 inventory get
//     per product, 10 max for 10 lines — inside 20.
//
// PRICING (Phase A, 2026-11-27 — per-product sale prices + fixed
// delivery fee, Model P: price = effective/charged price, optional
// display-only basePrice):
//   - Dual-shape window: an order may omit ALL THREE new order keys
//     (saleSavings, deliveryFee, amountDue) — that is an old-shape
//     order and it is valid. An order carrying ANY ONE of the three
//     must carry ALL THREE with all new invariants enforced; an
//     order carrying one without the other two is denied. Per line,
//     basePrice may be absent (old-shape line) or present (null = no
//     sale, or int >= price). Rollback returns the rules to exactly
//     this dual-shape version — a full revert to the pre-feature
//     exact-key rules is NOT the rollback path (it would reject
//     updates to orders created during the feature window).
//   - New invariants (when present): total == subtotal;
//     saleSavings == sum over lines of
//     (basePrice - price) * qty; amountDue == total + deliveryFee;
//     deliveryFee == the expected fee on ANONYMOUS storefront
//     creates only (decision D2 keeps the fee split — manual
//     orders are client-asserted, no fee get): the settings
//     deliveryFee when set, else 0 (unset fee = free, Mohamed's
//     decision 2026-11-27); 0 when total >= the settings
//     freeDeliveryThreshold, when set > 0 (D1 waiver, same
//     settings doc, no new get); basePrice ==
//     null || basePrice >= price per line.
//   - Product rule: basePrice == null || (basePrice is int &&
//     basePrice >= price); a fractional basePrice is denied.
//   - attemptId (string, optional) is present on storefront orders,
//     omitted on manual orders. Exact order keys: old shape 22–26,
//     new shape 25–30 (22 core + 3 money keys + optional
//     operationId + optional attemptId); per-line keys 4 or 5.
//     (Discount code REMOVED 2026-11-27: the three legacy code keys
//     discountCode/discountPercent/discountAmount stay in the
//     hasOnly allow-list with NO value checks, so orders created
//     while the code existed stay updatable — new orders omit them,
//     which is why the old-shape core is 22 keys, not 25.)
//   - Attempt docs (analytics/attempts/items) are shape-checked on
//     write (errorCode from the allowed set, seen values,
//     clientOrderId, plus the contact fields the live storefront
//     writes) — a fabricated doc that fails the shape check is
//     denied. The rejection-rate signal stays indicative-only (see
//     spec §11).
//
// inStock CROSS-CHECKS (contract §3 decision): the products-rule
// cross-check (productsInStockOk) is DROPPED — with both checks a
// 10-line stock-moving transaction costs 2N+1 > 20. The
// inventory-rule cross-check (inventoryInStockOk) is KEPT for
// authenticated admin/manager writes, and SKIPPED for anonymous
// writes (correction 2026-11-26): the anonymous order transaction
// reserves stock without updating products.inStock in the same
// transaction, so the check would deny reserving the last item
// (new availability 0 vs the stale inStock true). products.inStock
// is a display cache; its correctness is enforced indirectly.

rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    function isAdmin() {
      return request.auth != null
        && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/admins/$(request.auth.uid)).data.role == 'admin';
    }

    function isAdminOrManager() {
      return request.auth != null
        && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/admins/$(request.auth.uid)).data.role in ['admin', 'manager'];
    }

    /* The audit entry as projected after this request, or null when the
     * batch contains no such entry. */
    function auditAfter(opId) {
      return getAfter(/databases/$(database)/documents/audit/$(opId));
    }

    /* True when every key in `changed` is listed in the audit entry's
     * docIds entry for this document (subset coverage — see header). */
    function covers(changed, auditList) {
      return auditList != null
        && changed.intersection(auditList.toSet()).size() == changed.size();
    }

    /* True when this batch contains a valid audit entry for the change
     * to (collection, docId) with exactly `changed` keys changed:
     * actor + timestamp + the docIds index entry covering the change +
     * the per-document new values matching the written values for
     * every changed SENSITIVE field (T20: a fake audit that lists the
     * field but records a wrong new value is denied). The per-doc
     * values live in `newValuesByDoc` (keyed '<collection>/<docId>'):
     * a flat newValues map cannot hold two different values for the
     * same field when one operation touches several documents. */
    function hasAudit(opId, collection, docId, changed) {
      let entry = auditAfter(opId);
      let docIds = entry == null ? null : entry.data.get('docIds', null);
      return opId != null
        && entry != null
        && entry.data.get('actor', null) == request.auth.uid
        && entry.data.get('timestamp', null) == request.time
        && docIds != null
        && covers(changed, docIds[collection + '/' + docId])
        && sensitiveValuesOk(changed, entry, collection, docId);
    }

    /* Sensitive fields whose new value the audit entry must record
     * correctly (price, stock, reserved, status, paymentStatus,
     * inStock, percent — plus the pricing fields basePrice,
     * deliveryFee, saleSavings, amountDue, Phase A 2026-11-27). A
     * changed sensitive field with a missing or wrong recorded value
     * denies the write. */
    function sensitiveValuesOk(changed, entry, collection, docId) {
      let recorded = entry.data.newValuesByDoc != null
        ? entry.data.newValuesByDoc[collection + '/' + docId]
        : null;
      return (!('price' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.price == request.resource.data.price))
        && (!('stock' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.stock == request.resource.data.stock))
        && (!('reserved' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.reserved == request.resource.data.reserved))
        && (!('status' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.status == request.resource.data.status))
        && (!('paymentStatus' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.paymentStatus == request.resource.data.paymentStatus))
        && (!('inStock' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.inStock == request.resource.data.inStock))
        && (!('percent' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.percent == request.resource.data.percent))
        && (!('basePrice' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.basePrice == request.resource.data.basePrice))
        && (!('deliveryFee' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.deliveryFee == request.resource.data.deliveryFee))
        && (!('saleSavings' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.saleSavings == request.resource.data.saleSavings))
        && (!('amountDue' in changed) || (recorded != null && recorded.amountDue == request.resource.data.amountDue));
    }

    /* Changed keys for an update (diff against the stored doc). */
    function changedUpdate() {
      return request.resource.data.diff(resource.data).affectedKeys();
    }
    /* Changed keys for a create (every key of the new doc). */
    function changedCreate() {
      return request.resource.data.keys().toSet();
    }

    /* Delete audit id (deterministic — see header). */
    function deleteAuditId(collection, docId) {
      return 'del_' + collection + '_' + docId;
    }
    function hasDeleteAudit(collection, docId) {
      let entry = auditAfter(deleteAuditId(collection, docId));
      return entry != null
        && entry.data.get('actor', null) == request.auth.uid
        && entry.data.get('timestamp', null) == request.time
        && entry.data.get('operation', null) == 'delete'
        && entry.data.get('collection', null) == collection
        && entry.data.get('docId', null) == docId;
    }

    /* inStock must match the projected inventory (kept for
     * authenticated writes only — see header). Skipped while the
     * product has no inventory document or no inStock field (the
     * pre-migration window). */
    function inventoryInStockOk(productId) {
      let prod = getAfter(/databases/$(database)/documents/products/$(productId));
      return prod == null
        || !('inStock' in prod.data)
        || prod.data.inStock
          == ((request.resource.data.stock - request.resource.data.reserved) > 0);
    }

    /* The unified order state machine (v1.4 Decision 23). */
    function orderTransitionOk() {
      let from = resource.data.status;
      let to = request.resource.data.status;
      return from == to
        || (from == 'new' && to in ['accepted', 'cancelled', 'expired'])
        || (from == 'accepted' && to in ['preparing', 'cancelled'])
        || (from == 'preparing' && to in ['ready', 'cancelled'])
        || (from == 'ready' && to in ['in_transit', 'cancelled'])
        || (from == 'in_transit' && to == 'delivered')
        || (from == 'cancelled' && to == 'new');
    }

    /* ---- No-functions order helpers (contract §3) ---- */

    /* One order line: productId/name/price/qty, plus the optional
     * pricing basePrice (Phase A): an old-shape line has exactly the
     * 4 original keys; a new-shape line adds basePrice (5 keys) —
     * null when no sale, or an int >= price. A basePrice below the
     * charged price is a fake discount and is denied; a fractional
     * basePrice is denied (integer rule, same as the product rule).
     * price stays number, not int (correction 2026-11-26): a stored
     * fractional price must not deny a legitimate order whose line
     * price matches the DB exactly. Budget fix 2026-11-27: the
     * 4-or-5-key size check is gone — hasOnly + the field checks
     * below already deny a short line (a missing field errors or
     * fails its type check); the productId/name .size() > 0 checks
     * are gone too — an empty productId fails the DB price get in
     * linePriceOk, and name is display-only. Same verdicts. */
    function orderLineOk(item) {
      return item is map
        && item.keys().hasOnly(['productId', 'name', 'price', 'qty', 'basePrice'])
        && item.productId is string
        && item.name is string
        && item.price is number && item.price > 0
        && item.qty is int && item.qty >= 1 && item.qty <= 20
        && (!('basePrice' in item) || item.basePrice == null
          || (item.basePrice is int && item.basePrice >= item.price));
    }

    /* One traversal for shape + DB price + availability (budget fix
     * 2026-11-27): the old code walked the 10 slots THREE times
     * (orderLinesOk, orderPricesOk, orderAvailabilityOk), each with
     * its own size guard and items[i] fetch. Now a single
     * orderLineValue does shape + price get + availability get per
     * present line (M1: the validity walk is fused into the
     * subtotal sum via the poison value), with the size guard
     * hoisted to the call site so an absent slot costs one
     * comparison. Same checks, same gets (1 product get per line;
     * 1 inventory get per line only when the order has at most 3
     * lines — the OOS guard's 10-get budget note: worst case 3
     * price + 3 inventory + 1 fee = 7 (the code get is gone,
     * 2026-11-27; the audit getAfter left with the audit-split,
     * M1); larger orders keep the transaction + reserve-rule
     * guards, exactly as before). */
    function orderLineValid(i) {
      let items = request.resource.data.items;
      return orderLineOk(items[i])
        && linePriceOk(i)
        && (items.size() > 3 || lineAvailOk(i));
    }

    /* Line i's price must equal the products doc price (one get per
     * line — rules have no loop). Called only for i < items.size(),
     * after orderLineOk proved productId is a string. */
    function linePriceOk(i) {
      let items = request.resource.data.items;
      let prod = get(/databases/$(database)/documents/products/$(items[i].productId));
      return prod != null && prod.data.price == items[i].price;
    }

    /* Per-line availability guard [OOS]: qty <= stock - reserved on
     * the matching inventory doc — the backstop against a forged
     * order write that skips the transaction's stock re-check. Called
     * only for i < items.size() and only when the order has at most
     * 3 lines (see orderLineValid). */
    function lineAvailOk(i) {
      let items = request.resource.data.items;
      let inv = get(/databases/$(database)/documents/inventory/$(items[i].productId));
      return inv != null && items[i].qty <= (inv.data.get('stock', 0) - inv.data.get('reserved', 0));
    }

    /* POISON-VALUE line check (Option 1, M1 2026-11-27): the fused
     * validity + subtotal traversal. Returns price*qty of line i
     * when the line is valid (shape + DB price + availability, via
     * orderLineValid), otherwise the poison value -10^15. Validity
     * is then implied by the sum: a poisoned term makes the total
     * hugely negative, and subtotal >= 0 is enforced, so
     * subtotal == sum(lineValue) can never hold when any line is
     * invalid. Correct ONLY while no legitimate line value or
     * subtotal can be negative (prices and quantities are
     * non-negative, subtotal >= 0 is enforced) — if a future
     * change allows negative prices (e.g. a refund line), this
     * trick breaks silently: the dedicated poison test in
     * test/rules.test.js pins the behaviour. Unguarded —
     * orderSubtotalOk only calls it for i < items.size(). */
    function orderLineValue(i) {
      let items = request.resource.data.items;
      return orderLineValid(i) ? items[i].price * items[i].qty : -1000000000000000;
    }

    /* subtotal must equal the unrolled sum of price*qty (the rules
     * cannot loop). The sum runs over orderLineValue, so validity
     * is encoded in it (Option 1, M1 2026-11-27): the separate
     * orderLinesValid traversal is gone — a poisoned term from an
     * invalid line makes this sum mismatch, so this one check
     * proves both the subtotal AND that every present line is
     * valid. Added beyond the contract's letter — the contract
     * lists the total relation but not the subtotal
     * sum, and without it a forged low subtotal (with a matching
     * total) would pass. Costs 0 extra reads. */
    function orderSubtotalOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let n = d.items.size();
      return d.subtotal
        == (n <= 0 ? 0 : orderLineValue(0)) + (n <= 1 ? 0 : orderLineValue(1))
        + (n <= 2 ? 0 : orderLineValue(2)) + (n <= 3 ? 0 : orderLineValue(3))
        + (n <= 4 ? 0 : orderLineValue(4)) + (n <= 5 ? 0 : orderLineValue(5))
        + (n <= 6 ? 0 : orderLineValue(6)) + (n <= 7 ? 0 : orderLineValue(7))
        + (n <= 8 ? 0 : orderLineValue(8)) + (n <= 9 ? 0 : orderLineValue(9));
    }

    /* Per-line saving of line i (pricing Phase A): (basePrice -
     * price) * qty when the line carries a base price, else 0 — an
     * absent or null basePrice means no sale on that line and
     * contributes nothing. Exact integer math, never rounded. */
    function orderLineSaving(i) {
      let items = request.resource.data.items;
      return (!('basePrice' in items[i]) || items[i].basePrice == null) ? 0
        : (items[i].basePrice - items[i].price) * items[i].qty;
    }

    /* saleSavings must equal the unrolled sum of the per-line
     * savings (the rules cannot loop). */
    function orderSaleSavingsOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let n = d.items.size();
      return d.saleSavings
        == (n <= 0 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(0)) + (n <= 1 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(1))
        + (n <= 2 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(2)) + (n <= 3 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(3))
        + (n <= 4 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(4)) + (n <= 5 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(5))
        + (n <= 6 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(6)) + (n <= 7 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(7))
        + (n <= 8 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(8)) + (n <= 9 ? 0 : orderLineSaving(9));
    }

    /* The full order shape (contract §3 + pricing Phase A dual-shape):
     * exact keys, field types and ranges, totals consistent,
     * lifecycle fields null, timestamps == request.time, ids == the
     * doc id, createdBy matching the source. Dual-shape: an order may
     * omit ALL THREE new money keys (saleSavings, deliveryFee,
     * amountDue) — an old-shape order, valid at 22–26 keys. An order
     * carrying ANY ONE of the three must carry ALL THREE (new shape,
     * 25–30 keys: 22 core + 3 money keys + optional operationId +
     * optional attemptId) with all new invariants enforced. attemptId
     * on its own (without the three money keys) is denied. Per-line
     * basePrice may be absent (old-shape line) or present.
     * Discount code REMOVED 2026-11-27: the three legacy code keys
     * (discountCode, discountPercent, discountAmount) stay in the
     * hasOnly allow-list below with NO value checks, so orders
     * created while the code existed stay updatable — new orders
     * omit them, which is why the old-shape core is 22 keys, not
     * 25. total == subtotal (no discount subtracted any more).
     * Dual-shape contact (incomplete orders, 2026-11-27): either
     * money shape may also carry customerPhone2 (optional backup
     * phone), governorate (stable ID) and detailedAddress — 0 to 3
     * extra keys (old shape 22–26 keys, new-money shape 25–30).
     * customerAddress always carries the combined string. */
    function orderShapeOk(doc) {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let keys = d.keys();
      let hasMoney = 'saleSavings' in d || 'deliveryFee' in d || 'amountDue' in d;
      let hasAllMoney = 'saleSavings' in d && 'deliveryFee' in d && 'amountDue' in d;
      // operationId is OPTIONAL (PC manual orders stamp it; storefront
      // + Flutter omit it) — read it with .get(), never dot-access:
      // d.operationId ERRORS when the field is absent and denies every
      // storefront order (bug found from firestore-debug.log, 2026-11-27).
      let opId = d.get('operationId', null);
      return keys.hasOnly(['id', 'clientOrderId', 'customerName', 'customerPhone', 'customerPhone2', 'customerAddress', 'governorate', 'detailedAddress', 'items', 'subtotal', 'discountCode', 'discountPercent', 'discountAmount', 'total', 'status', 'paymentStatus', 'source', 'createdBy', 'shippingCompanyId', 'trackingNumber', 'notes', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt', 'acceptedAt', 'deliveredAt', 'cancelledAt', 'cancelReason', 'auditId', 'operationId', 'saleSavings', 'deliveryFee', 'amountDue', 'attemptId'])
        && ((!hasMoney && keys.size() >= 22 && keys.size() <= 26 && !('attemptId' in d))
          || (hasAllMoney && keys.size() >= 25 && keys.size() <= 30))
        && (opId == null || opId is string)
        && (!('customerPhone2' in d) || d.customerPhone2 == null || (d.customerPhone2 is string && d.customerPhone2.matches('^01[0125][0-9]{8}$')))
        && (!('governorate' in d) || d.governorate == null || (d.governorate is string && d.governorate.size() >= 1 && d.governorate.size() <= 50))
        && (!('detailedAddress' in d) || d.detailedAddress == null || (d.detailedAddress is string && d.detailedAddress.size() <= 500))
        /* 'operationId' is optional (coordinator fix 2026-11-26):
         * the PC manual order stamps it on the order doc; the
         * storefront + Flutter orders have exactly the 22 core
         * keys. The field is a harmless correlation id. */
        && d.id == doc && d.clientOrderId == doc
        && d.customerName is string && d.customerName.size() > 0
        && d.customerPhone is string && d.customerPhone.size() >= 10
        && d.customerAddress is string && d.customerAddress.size() > 0
        && d.items is list && d.items.size() >= 1 && d.items.size() <= 10
        && d.subtotal is number && d.subtotal >= 0
        && d.total is number && d.total >= 0
        && d.total == d.subtotal
        && orderSubtotalOk()
        && (!('saleSavings' in d) || (d.saleSavings is int && d.saleSavings >= 0 && orderSaleSavingsOk()))
        && (!('deliveryFee' in d) || (d.deliveryFee is int && d.deliveryFee >= 0))
        && (!('amountDue' in d) || (d.amountDue is int && d.amountDue >= 0 && d.amountDue == d.total + d.deliveryFee))
        && (!('attemptId' in d) || (d.attemptId is string && d.attemptId.size() > 0))
        && d.status == 'new' && d.paymentStatus == 'cod_pending'
        && d.source in ['storefront', 'admin_manual']
        && ((d.source == 'storefront' && d.createdBy == null)
          || (d.source == 'admin_manual' && request.auth != null && d.createdBy == request.auth.uid))
        && d.acceptedAt == null && d.deliveredAt == null
        && d.cancelledAt == null && d.cancelReason == null
        && (d.shippingCompanyId == null || d.shippingCompanyId is string)
        && (d.trackingNumber == null || d.trackingNumber is string)
        && (d.notes == null || d.notes is string)
        && d.createdAt == request.time && d.updatedAt == request.time;
    }

    /* REMOVED by the audit-split (M1 2026-11-27, approved):
     * orderAuditOk verified the order's audit entry via getAfter.
     * The order rule no longer checks it — the audit is written
     * by the client after the order commits (best-effort). Kept
     * in git history; do not re-add without a design decision. */

    /* Delivery-fee verification (pricing §4, decision D2 — the fee
     * split): ANONYMOUS storefront creates only. The rule reads
     * storeSettings/settings once (1 get, counted in the header
     * table) and requires deliveryFee to equal the expected fee.
     * Expected fee (fix round 2026-11-27, Mohamed's decision
     * ~12:23): the settings `deliveryFee` when it is set (int >= 0),
     * else 0 — an unset fee means FREE delivery, never a denial.
     * D1 (same round): when `freeDeliveryThreshold` (read from the
     * SAME settings doc — no new get) is set (> 0) and the order
     * `total` reaches it, the fee is waived: expected fee is 0.
     * Manual orders are client-asserted and pay no fee get; old-shape
     * orders carry no deliveryFee and pay no fee get either. */
    function orderFeeOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let settings = (request.auth == null && d.source == 'storefront' && 'deliveryFee' in d)
        ? get(/databases/$(database)/documents/storeSettings/settings) : null;
      let rawFee = settings == null ? null : settings.data.get('deliveryFee', null);
      let fee = rawFee is int && rawFee >= 0 ? rawFee : 0;
      let rawThreshold = settings == null ? null : settings.data.get('freeDeliveryThreshold', null);
      let waived = rawThreshold is int && rawThreshold > 0 && d.total >= rawThreshold;
      return request.auth != null || d.source != 'storefront' || !('deliveryFee' in d)
        || d.deliveryFee == (waived ? 0 : fee);
    }

    /* Manual orders: admin, or manager with orders_create_manual.
     * (1 get, cached with the role checks in the same request.) */
    function manualOrderAllowed() {
      let admin = get(/databases/$(database)/documents/admins/$(request.auth.uid));
      let perms = admin == null ? null : admin.data.get('permissions', null);
      return admin != null
        && (admin.data.get('role', null) == 'admin'
          || (admin.data.get('role', null) == 'manager'
            && perms != null
            && perms.get('orders_create_manual', false) == true));
    }

    /* Product base price (pricing Phase A, Model P): absent or null
     * means no sale; when present it must be an int >= price. A
     * basePrice below the charged price is a fake discount and is
     * denied; a fractional basePrice is denied. Applies to the
     * merged document on update, so raising price above a stored
     * basePrice is denied too — clear the basePrice in the same
     * write. */
    function productBasePriceOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return !('basePrice' in d) || d.basePrice == null
        || (d.basePrice is int && d.basePrice >= d.price);
    }

    /* Attempt-doc shape (pricing §11 / M21 + Phase C corrections
     * 2026-11-27): the doc carries exactly the attempt fields with
     * the right types. startedAt + ordered are always present (the
     * storefront writes them at checkout open); errorCode is from
     * the allowed set or absent — the set includes FEE_UNSET (the
     * storefront used to throw it when the fee was missing; the
     * fee-default-free change 2026-11-27 removed the throw, and the
     * code stays allowed here so older clients' attempt writes
     * still pass; it was missing from the spec §11 set); seen values are int maps (seenPrices /
     * seenBasePrices) or the seen scalar fee (seenDeliveryFee, int)
     * / seen amount due (seenTotal, number — the amount due the
     * customer saw); currentPrices / currentBasePrices are the
     * current database prices the transaction returned (int maps)
     * and currentFee is the current fee (int) — the "current
     * database prices" failure field §11 named without a field name,
     * now named by the live storefront (recordAttemptFailure);
     * clientOrderId is a string or absent; contactName/Phone/Address
     * are the contact fields the live storefront writes at the info
     * step (Decision 19 still open — they stay allowed here, or the
     * info-step update would be denied). The rules language cannot
     * iterate map values, so the int-ness of individual seen-map
     * entries is NOT checkable here — the map-type check is the
     * enforceable part. */
    function attemptShapeOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['startedAt', 'ordered', 'errorCode', 'seenPrices', 'seenBasePrices', 'seenTotal', 'seenDeliveryFee', 'currentPrices', 'currentBasePrices', 'currentFee', 'clientOrderId', 'contactName', 'contactPhone', 'contactAddress'])
        && d.get('startedAt', null) is timestamp
        && d.get('ordered', null) is bool
        && (!('errorCode' in d) || d.errorCode == null || d.errorCode in ['PRICE_CHANGED', 'FEE_CHANGED', 'TOTAL_CHANGED', 'INSUFFICIENT_STOCK', 'FEE_UNSET', 'permission-denied'])
        && (!('seenPrices' in d) || d.seenPrices == null || d.seenPrices is map)
        && (!('seenBasePrices' in d) || d.seenBasePrices == null || d.seenBasePrices is map)
        && (!('seenTotal' in d) || d.seenTotal == null || d.seenTotal is number)
        && (!('seenDeliveryFee' in d) || d.seenDeliveryFee == null || d.seenDeliveryFee is int)
        && (!('currentPrices' in d) || d.currentPrices == null || d.currentPrices is map)
        && (!('currentBasePrices' in d) || d.currentBasePrices == null || d.currentBasePrices is map)
        && (!('currentFee' in d) || d.currentFee == null || d.currentFee is int)
        && (!('clientOrderId' in d) || d.clientOrderId == null || (d.clientOrderId is string && d.clientOrderId.size() > 0))
        && (!('contactName' in d) || d.contactName == null || d.contactName is string)
        && (!('contactPhone' in d) || d.contactPhone == null || d.contactPhone is string)
        && (!('contactAddress' in d) || d.contactAddress == null || d.contactAddress is string);
    }

    /* Pure stock reservation (contract §1): the order transaction
     * reserves stock without an audit entry and without updating
     * products.inStock in the same write. The contract §3 says the
     * inventory rule is "unchanged" (admin/manager + audit), but
     * that cannot stand as written: the anonymous storefront
     * transaction and the authenticated manual transaction both
     * write inventory with no operationId and no audit entry, so
     * under the old rule every order would be denied. This branch
     * is the minimal fix: allowed for ANY requester (anonymous
     * storefront or authenticated manual order) ONLY when the write
     * strictly increases reserved, leaves stock and the other
     * fields untouched, keeps reserved <= stock, and stamps
     * updatedAt. The inStock cross-check is SKIPPED here
     * (correction 2026-11-26): products.inStock is refreshed by
     * the §13 second write, so reserving the last item would
     * otherwise be denied against the stale flag. No audit coverage
     * is required here (correction 2026-11-26): the storefront's
     * audit entry covers ONLY the order doc (docIds
     * {'orders/{id}': ['status','total']}), never the inventory
     * writes — value/shape validation is the whole check.
     * Consequence, accepted per contract §12: an anonymous client
     * can set reserved up to stock on any product (a bounded
     * stock-DoS, released by the lazy sweep / admin cancel); there
     * is no rules mechanism for it, so it is not fixed here.
     * Releases (reserved down) and stock changes still need the
     * audited admin branch. Costs 0 access calls. */
    /* Reserve slimming (M1 2026-11-27, Step 3 — measured: after
     * Option 1 + audit-split + Option 3, the 1-line sale+fee order
     * fits but 2/7/8-line orders still die max-expr, and the debug
     * log shows the deaths inside the per-line validity traversal
     * that runs after the reserves — so the reserves themselves
     * must get cheaper). Four conjuncts are dropped: the redundant
     * `stock >= 0` (stock is pinned to the stored value, which was
     * validated when written), and the `productId` / `minStock` /
     * `costPrice` pins (fields the reserve write only echoes back
     * unchanged — nothing in the order flow reads them from the
     * request, and a wrong echo can no longer deny a legitimate
     * reserve). Kept: doc exists, reserved is a non-negative int,
     * stock equals the stored stock, reserved strictly increases
     * within stock, updatedAt == request.time. The stock itself is
     * still protected: reserved can only move up, never past stock. */
    function inventoryReserveOk(doc) {
      let old = resource == null ? null : resource.data;
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let newReserved = d.get('reserved', null);
      return resource != null
        && newReserved is int && newReserved >= 0
        && d.get('stock', 0) == old.get('stock', 0)
        && newReserved > old.get('reserved', 0)
        && newReserved <= d.get('stock', 0)
        && d.get('updatedAt', null) == request.time;
    }
    /* Budget fix 2026-11-27: the changedUpdate().hasOnly([...])
     * conjunct is gone. The fields it guarded that still matter
     * (stock / reserved equal the stored values, updatedAt ==
     * request.time, reserved strictly increases within stock) are
     * pinned by a value check above, so the hasOnly only blocked
     * inert extra fields — at the price of a full diff() per
     * reserve, which blew the 1000-expression budget on multi-line
     * orders. The productId / minStock / costPrice pins are gone
     * too (reserve slimming, Step 3 — see the comment above the
     * function): those fields are only echoed back by the reserve
     * write. 'operationId' stays tolerated (the Flutter + PC manual
     * orders stamp it; it is a harmless correlation id, and without
     * it those apps fall back to the audited admin branch
     * (2 reads/line) and a 6-line manual order breaks the
     * per-request budget). The value checks above still protect
     * the stock. */

    /* §13 inStock refresh (correction 2026-11-26): a batched merge
     * setting ONLY inStock, verified against the inventory doc
     * (1 get). No audit entry — the value is derived from
     * inventory, the ground truth. Allowed for any requester: the
     * anonymous storefront refresh and the authenticated admin-app
     * refresh are the same verified write (an admin-app refresh
     * denied for lack of audit would leave the storefront showing
     * stale availability after a manual order). */
    function productsRefreshOk(doc) {
      let flag = request.resource.data.get('inStock', null);
      let inv = changedUpdate().hasOnly(['inStock']) ? get(/databases/$(database)/documents/inventory/$(doc)) : null;
      return changedUpdate().hasOnly(['inStock'])
        && inv != null
        && flag is bool
        && flag == ((inv.data.get('stock', 0) - inv.data.get('reserved', 0)) > 0);
    }

    /* Anonymous stock-movement entry for an order (contract §3):
     * the exact 7-field shape, reserve types only (negative qty). */
    function movementReserveOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let keys = d.keys();
      return request.auth == null
        && keys.hasOnly(['productId', 'type', 'qty', 'orderId', 'source', 'actorUid', 'createdAt'])
        && keys.size() == 7
        && d.productId is string && d.productId.size() > 0
        && d.type in ['order_reserve', 'reopen_reserve']
        && d.qty is int && d.qty < 0
        && d.orderId is string && d.orderId.size() > 0
        && d.source in ['placeOrder', 'createManualOrder']
        && (d.actorUid == null || d.actorUid is string)
        && d.createdAt == request.time;
    }

    /* One-way complaint card (contract §3/§6): the exact 5-field
     * shape. Any requester — the anonymous storefront form and an
     * admin filing on a customer's behalf write the same fields,
     * with no audit entry. Incomplete orders (2026-11-27) add an
     * optional sixth field, `source`: 'direct' (the contact form /
     * admin filing — the old 5-field shape, source absent, means
     * direct) | 'exit-feedback' (desktop exit popup) |
     * 'footer-feedback' (footer link). Name and phone stay required
     * for direct, but may be empty for exit/footer feedback — the
     * visitor may answer anonymously. The message stays required
     * (10–2000 chars) in every shape. */
    function feedbackOneWayOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let src = d.get('source', 'direct');
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['name', 'email', 'phone', 'message', 'createdAt', 'source'])
        && (d.keys().size() == 5 || d.keys().size() == 6)
        && src in ['direct', 'exit-feedback', 'footer-feedback']
        && d.name is string && d.name.size() <= 100
        && (src != 'direct' || d.name.size() > 0)
        && d.email is string && d.email.size() <= 100 && (d.email == '' || d.email.matches('.*@.*'))
        && d.phone is string
        && (src != 'direct' || d.phone.matches('[0-9]{10,15}'))
        && (src == 'direct' || d.phone == '' || d.phone.matches('[0-9]{10,15}'))
        && d.message is string && d.message.size() >= 10 && d.message.size() <= 2000
        && d.createdAt == request.time;
    }

    /* ---- Incomplete orders: checkout drafts (2026-11-27) ----
     * One document per browser session (doc id == sessionId). The
     * storefront owns the document while the visitor types; admins
     * own it after that (status, conversion, delete). Anonymous
     * read and list are denied. Anonymous create needs a non-empty
     * session token; anonymous update needs the incoming token to
     * equal the stored token, the token itself unchanged, and the
     * admin-owned fields (status, orderId, mootOrderId) unchanged.
     * The schema is docs/incomplete-orders-schema.md. */
    function draftCartLineOkAt(i) {
      let cart = request.resource.data.get('cart', []);
      return cart.size() <= i
        || (cart[i] is map
          && cart[i].keys().hasOnly(['productId', 'qty', 'priceAtDraft', 'availability', 'availableQty'])
          && cart[i].productId is string && cart[i].productId.size() > 0
          && cart[i].qty is int && cart[i].qty >= 1 && cart[i].qty <= 20
          && cart[i].priceAtDraft is number && cart[i].priceAtDraft >= 0
          && cart[i].availability in ['ok', 'out', 'short']
          && cart[i].availableQty is int && cart[i].availableQty >= 0);
    }

    function draftCartOk() {
      return draftCartLineOkAt(0) && draftCartLineOkAt(1) && draftCartLineOkAt(2)
        && draftCartLineOkAt(3) && draftCartLineOkAt(4) && draftCartLineOkAt(5)
        && draftCartLineOkAt(6) && draftCartLineOkAt(7) && draftCartLineOkAt(8)
        && draftCartLineOkAt(9) && draftCartLineOkAt(10) && draftCartLineOkAt(11)
        && draftCartLineOkAt(12) && draftCartLineOkAt(13) && draftCartLineOkAt(14)
        && draftCartLineOkAt(15) && draftCartLineOkAt(16) && draftCartLineOkAt(17)
        && draftCartLineOkAt(18) && draftCartLineOkAt(19);
    }

    function draftShapeOk(doc) {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['sessionId', 'sessionToken', 'name', 'phone', 'phone2', 'governorate', 'detailedAddress', 'address', 'cart', 'status', 'completeness', 'orderId', 'mootOrderId', 'lastSyncAt', 'createdAt', 'schemaVersion', 'operationId', 'updatedAt'])
        && d.sessionId == doc
        && d.sessionToken is string && d.sessionToken.size() > 0 && d.sessionToken.size() <= 128
        && d.name is string && d.name.size() <= 100
        && d.phone is string && (d.phone == '' || d.phone.matches('^01[0125][0-9]{8}$'))
        && (d.get('phone2', null) == null || (d.get('phone2', null) is string && (d.get('phone2', null) == '' || d.get('phone2', null).matches('^01[0125][0-9]{8}$'))))
        && (d.get('governorate', null) == null || (d.get('governorate', null) is string && d.get('governorate', null).size() <= 50))
        && (d.get('detailedAddress', null) == null || (d.get('detailedAddress', null) is string && d.get('detailedAddress', null).size() <= 500))
        && d.address is string && d.address.size() <= 500
        && d.cart is list && d.cart.size() <= 20
        && draftCartOk()
        && d.status in ['new', 'contacted', 'no-answer', 'converted', 'dead']
        && d.completeness is int && d.completeness >= 0 && d.completeness <= 100
        && (d.get('orderId', null) == null || d.get('orderId', null) is string)
        && (d.get('mootOrderId', null) == null || d.get('mootOrderId', null) is string)
        && d.lastSyncAt is timestamp && d.createdAt is timestamp
        && d.schemaVersion == 1;
    }

    function draftAnonUpdateOk(doc) {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return request.auth == null
        && resource.data.sessionToken == d.sessionToken
        && d.sessionId == resource.data.sessionId
        && d.status == resource.data.status
        && d.get('orderId', null) == resource.data.get('orderId', null)
        && d.get('mootOrderId', null) == resource.data.get('mootOrderId', null)
        && draftShapeOk(doc);
    }

    /* ---- Incomplete orders: journey summaries (2026-11-27) ----
     * One capped summary per browser session (doc id == sessionId).
     * Anonymous create/update only on the own session document
     * (sessionId == doc id, never changed); anonymous read and list
     * are denied. Dwell is stored in bands only, never per-second.
     * The schema is docs/incomplete-orders-schema.md. */
    function journeyEntryOkAt(i) {
      let products = request.resource.data.get('products', []);
      return products.size() <= i
        || (products[i] is map
          && products[i].keys().hasOnly(['productId', 'dwellBand', 'actions'])
          && products[i].productId is string && products[i].productId.size() > 0
          && products[i].dwellBand in ['<10s', '10-60s', '>60s']
          && products[i].actions is list && products[i].actions.size() <= 10);
    }

    function journeyEntriesOk() {
      return journeyEntryOkAt(0) && journeyEntryOkAt(1) && journeyEntryOkAt(2)
        && journeyEntryOkAt(3) && journeyEntryOkAt(4) && journeyEntryOkAt(5)
        && journeyEntryOkAt(6) && journeyEntryOkAt(7) && journeyEntryOkAt(8)
        && journeyEntryOkAt(9) && journeyEntryOkAt(10) && journeyEntryOkAt(11)
        && journeyEntryOkAt(12) && journeyEntryOkAt(13) && journeyEntryOkAt(14)
        && journeyEntryOkAt(15) && journeyEntryOkAt(16) && journeyEntryOkAt(17)
        && journeyEntryOkAt(18) && journeyEntryOkAt(19);
    }

    function journeyShapeOk(doc) {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['sessionId', 'draftId', 'orderId', 'startedAt', 'totalSecondsBand', 'products', 'overflowCount', 'updatedAt', 'schemaVersion'])
        && d.sessionId == doc
        && (d.get('draftId', null) == null || d.get('draftId', null) is string)
        && (d.get('orderId', null) == null || d.get('orderId', null) is string)
        && d.startedAt is timestamp && d.updatedAt is timestamp
        && (d.get('totalSecondsBand', null) == null || d.get('totalSecondsBand', null) in ['<10s', '10-60s', '>60s'])
        && d.products is list && d.products.size() <= 20
        && journeyEntriesOk()
        && d.overflowCount is int && d.overflowCount >= 0
        && d.schemaVersion == 1;
    }

    /* ---- Incomplete orders: governorate list + deletion config ----
     * The generic storeSettings match below allows public read and
     * audited admin writes; these shape checks ride on top of it
     * for the two new documents (admin-only writes — the shape is
     * enforced on top of the audit requirement, not instead of it).
     * Per-entry shape (stable id + boolean active) is enforced by
     * the admin clients and the seed script; the rules enforce the
     * list size (at most 27) and the deletion day range. */
    function governoratesShapeOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['entries', 'updatedAt', 'operationId'])
        && d.entries is list && d.entries.size() <= 27;
    }

    function deletionShapeOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return !('autoDeleteDays' in d)
        || (d.autoDeleteDays is int && d.autoDeleteDays >= 0 && d.autoDeleteDays <= 365);
    }

    /* ---- Templates: bundle registry + activation pointer (2026-11-27,
     * spec entries 10/18-22) ----
     * Registry shape (templates/{id}): the manifest copy {id, nameAr,
     * nameEn, version, shellMinVersion, bundleHash}, status in the
     * canonical SIX-state enum (draft | preview | approved | active |
     * retired — no 'validating', no 'awaiting-approval', no
     * 'archived'), the approval record, and the Hosting body path.
     * Activation history lives ONLY in the subcollection
     * templates/{id}/activations/{operationId} — NEVER a growing list
     * inside the registry doc (no 'history' key is allowed here).
     * The classic bundle is pinned: it can never be retired or
     * deleted while it is the rollback target — its status must stay
     * 'active' and its delete is denied outright. */
    function templateApprovalOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let a = d.get('approval', null);
      // The timestamp key is 'timestamp' per the spec/task; the admin
      // app's approveTemplate writes 'at' (entry 12). Both are
      // accepted until the coordinator normalises the name — exactly
      // one of them must be present, timestamp-typed. Flagged in the
      // entry-10 report; do NOT add a third spelling.
      let ts = a == null ? null : (a.get('timestamp', null) != null ? a.get('timestamp', null) : a.get('at', null));
      return a == null
        || (a is map
          && a.keys().hasOnly(['approver', 'timestamp', 'at', 'shellVersion', 'bundleHash'])
          && a.keys().size() == 4
          && ((('timestamp' in a) && !('at' in a)) || (('at' in a) && !('timestamp' in a)))
          && a.approver is string && a.approver.size() > 0
          && ts is timestamp
          && a.shellVersion is string && a.shellVersion.size() > 0
          && a.bundleHash is string && a.bundleHash.matches('^[0-9a-f]{64}$')
          && a.bundleHash == d.get('bundleHash', null));
    }

    function templateShapeOk(doc) {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['id', 'nameAr', 'nameEn', 'version', 'shellMinVersion', 'bundleHash', 'status', 'approval', 'previewImageUrl', 'bodyPath', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt', 'operationId'])
        && d.get('id', null) == doc
        && d.get('id', null) in ['bazaar', 'gallery', 'scroll', 'speclab', 'boutique', 'classic']
        && d.get('nameAr', null) is string && d.get('nameAr', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('nameEn', null) is string && d.get('nameEn', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('version', null) is string && d.get('version', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('shellMinVersion', null) is string && d.get('shellMinVersion', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('bundleHash', null) is string && d.get('bundleHash', null).matches('^[0-9a-f]{64}$')
        && d.get('status', null) in ['draft', 'preview', 'approved', 'active', 'retired']
        && templateApprovalOk()
        && (d.get('previewImageUrl', null) == null || d.get('previewImageUrl', null) is string)
        && (d.get('bodyPath', null) == null || d.get('bodyPath', null) is string);
    }

    /* The status machine: draft -> preview -> approved -> active, with
     * retire from any non-retired state and preview as the way back
     * from approved. Same-status writes are metadata edits. Skipping
     * a step (draft -> approved/active, preview -> active) and
     * un-activating to draft/preview are denied; retired is terminal.
     * active -> approved IS allowed: it is how the template that
     * stops being live returns to standby with its approval kept
     * (the activation flow writes it in the same batch as the
     * pointer flip — entry 12). Classic alone may go draft -> active
     * (its seed path — the live site is its own approval). Re-approval
     * exception (fix 2026-11-27 — this contradicted templateFrozenOk,
     * which REQUIRES a drop to draft when the hash/version/shell
     * changes): approved -> draft IS allowed when a frozen field
     * changed; templateFrozenOk still requires the approval record
     * to be removed on that path, and approved -> draft with NO
     * frozen change stays denied. */
    function templateStatusTransitionOk(doc) {
      let from = resource.data.get('status', null);
      let to = request.resource.data.get('status', null);
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let frozenChanged = d.get('bundleHash', null) != resource.data.get('bundleHash', null)
        || d.get('version', null) != resource.data.get('version', null)
        || d.get('shellMinVersion', null) != resource.data.get('shellMinVersion', null);
      return from == to
        || (from == 'draft' && to in ['preview', 'retired'])
        || (from == 'preview' && to in ['approved', 'draft', 'retired'])
        || (from == 'approved' && to in ['active', 'preview', 'retired'])
        || (from == 'approved' && to == 'draft' && frozenChanged)
        || (from == 'active' && to in ['approved', 'retired'])
        || (doc == 'classic' && from == 'draft' && to == 'active');
    }

    /* Approval freezes the bundle: changing the hash, the version, or
     * the minimum shell version voids the approval — the write must
     * drop back to draft with the approval record removed, and the
     * bundle must be approved again. (The hash half is also enforced
     * by templateApprovalOk: a kept approval whose bundleHash no
     * longer matches the doc is denied.) */
    function templateFrozenOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let frozenChanged = d.get('bundleHash', null) != resource.data.get('bundleHash', null)
        || d.get('version', null) != resource.data.get('version', null)
        || d.get('shellMinVersion', null) != resource.data.get('shellMinVersion', null);
      return !frozenChanged
        || (d.get('status', null) == 'draft' && d.get('approval', null) == null);
    }

    /* The activation pointer (storeSettings/activeTemplate): templateId
     * + bundleVersion + bundleHash + previousTemplateId (display only
     * — NEVER the rollback source) + the append-only history stack.
     * The admin app also stamps activatedBy/activatedAt on the pointer
     * (entry 12) — allowed, never required. The last history entry
     * must be the activation this write records (template + version
     * + hash + time + admin). */
    function pointerShapeOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let history = d.get('history', null);
      let last = history is list && history.size() >= 1 ? history[history.size() - 1] : null;
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['templateId', 'bundleVersion', 'bundleHash', 'previousTemplateId', 'history', 'activatedBy', 'activatedAt', 'operationId', 'updatedAt'])
        && d.get('templateId', null) is string && d.get('templateId', null) in ['bazaar', 'gallery', 'scroll', 'speclab', 'boutique', 'classic']
        && d.get('bundleVersion', null) is string && d.get('bundleVersion', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('bundleHash', null) is string && d.get('bundleHash', null).matches('^[0-9a-f]{64}$')
        && d.get('previousTemplateId', null) is string
        && (d.get('activatedBy', null) == null || d.get('activatedBy', null) is string)
        && (d.get('activatedAt', null) == null || d.get('activatedAt', null) is timestamp)
        && history is list && history.size() >= 1
        && last is map
        && last.get('templateId', null) == d.get('templateId', null)
        && last.get('bundleVersion', null) == d.get('bundleVersion', null)
        && last.get('bundleHash', null) == d.get('bundleHash', null)
        && last.get('at', null) is timestamp
        && last.get('by', null) is string && last.get('by', null).size() > 0;
    }

    /* The referenced template must be 'active' at write time — a
     * pointer to a draft / preview / approved / retired template is
     * denied, so a rollback to an archived-or-retired template is
     * denied too and the client restores classic instead (1 getAfter,
     * the same cost as the old templateId check it replaces for this
     * doc). A missing target doc denies (null .data errors). */
    function pointerTargetActiveOk() {
      return getAfter(/databases/$(database)/documents/templates/$(request.resource.data.templateId)).data.status == 'active';
    }

    /* Pointer create: full shape + the target is active. */
    function pointerCreateOk() {
      return pointerShapeOk() && pointerTargetActiveOk();
    }

    /* Pointer update: the history stack grows by exactly one entry
     * (append-only — no rewrite, no truncation), previousTemplateId
     * records the template that was live before this write (display
     * only), and the target is active. */
    function pointerUpdateOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let history = d.get('history', null);
      let oldHistory = resource.data.get('history', null);
      return pointerShapeOk()
        && history is list && oldHistory is list
        && history.size() == oldHistory.size() + 1
        && d.get('previousTemplateId', null) == resource.data.get('templateId', null)
        && pointerTargetActiveOk();
    }

    /* One activation-history entry (templates/{id}/activations/{op}):
     * append-only, admin-written, shaped exactly. The admin app also
     * stamps its own operation id into the doc ('operationId' == the
     * document id, entry 12) — allowed, never required. */
    function activationShapeOk(doc, operationId) {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['templateId', 'bundleVersion', 'bundleHash', 'shellVersion', 'approver', 'at', 'action', 'operationId'])
        && (d.keys().size() == 7 || d.keys().size() == 8)
        && d.get('templateId', null) == doc
        && (d.get('operationId', null) == null || d.get('operationId', null) == operationId)
        && d.get('bundleVersion', null) is string && d.get('bundleVersion', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('bundleHash', null) is string && d.get('bundleHash', null).matches('^[0-9a-f]{64}$')
        && d.get('shellVersion', null) is string && d.get('shellVersion', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('approver', null) is string && d.get('approver', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('at', null) == request.time
        && d.get('action', null) in ['activate', 'rollback', 'retire'];
    }

    /* A preview slug (previews/{slug}): what ?preview=<slug> resolves
     * through. Shape is the admin app's slug record (entry 12):
     * {templateId, version, issuedAt, issuedBy, status}. Anonymous
     * get only, never list; admin-only writes. The slug issue/revoke
     * calls are direct Firestore writes (no audit entry — the slug
     * document itself is the record), so create/update carry no audit
     * requirement; the admin list is allowed because rotation queries
     * the open slugs for a template. */
    function previewShapeOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return d.keys().hasOnly(['templateId', 'version', 'issuedAt', 'issuedBy', 'status'])
        && d.keys().size() == 5
        && d.get('templateId', null) is string && d.get('templateId', null) in ['bazaar', 'gallery', 'scroll', 'speclab', 'boutique', 'classic']
        && d.get('version', null) is string && d.get('version', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('issuedAt', null) is timestamp
        && d.get('issuedBy', null) is string && d.get('issuedBy', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('status', null) in ['open', 'revoked'];
    }

    /* Homepage promo banners (D2): a banner's endDate, when present,
     * must be a valid date-time — an ISO 8601 string (the shape the
     * admin editor writes; '' means "no end date") or a Firestore
     * timestamp. The rules cannot loop, so the first 20 banners are
     * unrolled; banners past the 20th are unchecked (documented gap
     * — the editor holds far fewer). Budget fix 2026-11-27: the
     * size guard lives at the CALL site (banners.size() <= i), so
     * an absent slot costs one comparison, not a function call
     * that re-fetches the list — the old shape blew the
     * 1000-expression budget on a 1-banner write. */
    function bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, i) {
      let slot = banners[i] is map ? banners[i] : null;
      let end = slot == null ? null : slot.get('endDate', null);
      return slot == null
        || end == null || end == ''
        || end is timestamp
        || (end is string && end.matches('^\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])T([01][0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-5][0-9](:[0-5][0-9])?(\\.\\d+)?(Z|[+-]([01][0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-5][0-9])$'));
    }

    function homepagePromoBannersOk() {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      let banners = d.get('promoBanners', null);
      return banners == null || (banners is list
        && (banners.size() <= 0 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 0))
        && (banners.size() <= 1 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 1))
        && (banners.size() <= 2 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 2))
        && (banners.size() <= 3 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 3))
        && (banners.size() <= 4 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 4))
        && (banners.size() <= 5 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 5))
        && (banners.size() <= 6 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 6))
        && (banners.size() <= 7 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 7))
        && (banners.size() <= 8 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 8))
        && (banners.size() <= 9 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 9))
        && (banners.size() <= 10 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 10))
        && (banners.size() <= 11 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 11))
        && (banners.size() <= 12 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 12))
        && (banners.size() <= 13 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 13))
        && (banners.size() <= 14 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 14))
        && (banners.size() <= 15 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 15))
        && (banners.size() <= 16 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 16))
        && (banners.size() <= 17 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 17))
        && (banners.size() <= 18 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 18))
        && (banners.size() <= 19 || bannerEndDateOkAt(banners, 19)));
    }

    /* Anonymous audit entry for a storefront order (contract §3):
     * shape-only, no get() — a fake entry is noise in an
     * admin-read-only log, not a money/stock issue. Audit-split
     * (M1 2026-11-27): the ORDER rule no longer verifies this
     * entry via getAfter — it is written best-effort after the
     * order commits, and the admin orphan-order repair is the
     * backstop for a missing one. */
    function auditAnonOk(operationId) {
      let d = request.resource.data;
      return request.auth == null
        && d.get('actor', null) in ['anonymous', 'storefront']
        && d.get('docId', null) is string && d.get('docId', null).size() > 0
        && d.get('operationId', null) == operationId
        && d.get('timestamp', null) == request.time
        && d.get('collection', null) == 'orders'
        && d.get('operation', null) in ['create', 'manual_order_create']
        && d.get('docIds', null) is map && d.get('docIds', null).size() == 1
        && d.get('docIds', null).keys().hasOnly(['orders/' + d.get('docId', null)])
        && d.get('newValuesByDoc', null) is map && d.get('newValuesByDoc', null).size() == 1
        && d.get('newValuesByDoc', null).keys().hasOnly(['orders/' + d.get('docId', null)]);
    }

    // ---- Public storefront content ----
    // storeSettings/activeTemplate is the activation pointer (see the
    // pointer helpers above): full shape + append-only history +
    // target 'active'. storeSettings/homepage carries the D2 endDate
    // validation on its promo banners. Every other settings doc keeps
    // the old behaviour (public read, audited admin write). ----
    match /storeSettings/{doc} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create: if isAdmin()
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'storeSettings', doc, changedCreate())
        && (doc != 'governorates' || governoratesShapeOk())
        && (doc != 'deletion' || deletionShapeOk())
        && (doc != 'homepage' || homepagePromoBannersOk())
        && (doc != 'activeTemplate' || pointerCreateOk())
        && (doc == 'activeTemplate'
          || (!('templateId' in request.resource.data)
            || getAfter(/databases/$(database)/documents/templates/$(request.resource.data.templateId)).data.status == 'active'));
      allow update: if isAdmin()
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'storeSettings', doc, changedUpdate())
        && (doc != 'governorates' || governoratesShapeOk())
        && (doc != 'deletion' || deletionShapeOk())
        && (doc != 'homepage' || homepagePromoBannersOk())
        && (doc != 'activeTemplate' || pointerUpdateOk())
        && (doc == 'activeTemplate'
          || (!('templateId' in request.resource.data)
            || getAfter(/databases/$(database)/documents/templates/$(request.resource.data.templateId)).data.status == 'active'));
      allow delete: if isAdmin() && hasDeleteAudit('storeSettings', doc);
    }

    // ---- Checkout drafts (incomplete orders, 2026-11-27): deny
    // anonymous read and list; anonymous create/update only on the
    // document the session owns (token check); admin read/list/
    // update, admin-only delete with a delete-audit. ----
    match /checkoutDrafts/{doc} {
      allow get, list: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if request.auth == null
        && draftShapeOk(doc)
        && request.resource.data.status == 'new'
        && request.resource.data.get('orderId', null) == null
        && request.resource.data.get('mootOrderId', null) == null;
      allow update: if isAdminOrManager()
        || (request.auth == null && draftAnonUpdateOk(doc));
      allow delete: if isAdmin() && hasDeleteAudit('checkoutDrafts', doc);
    }

    // ---- Journey summaries (incomplete orders, 2026-11-27): deny
    // anonymous read and list; anonymous create/update only on the
    // own session document; admin read/list/update, admin delete. ----
    match /journeySummaries/{doc} {
      allow get, list: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if request.auth == null && journeyShapeOk(doc);
      allow update: if isAdminOrManager()
        || (request.auth == null
          && resource.data.sessionId == request.resource.data.sessionId
          && journeyShapeOk(doc));
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    match /categories/{doc} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create: if isAdmin()
        && request.resource.data.name is string
        && request.resource.data.name.size() > 0
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'categories', doc, changedCreate());
      allow update: if isAdmin()
        && (!('name' in request.resource.data)
          || (request.resource.data.name is string && request.resource.data.name.size() > 0))
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'categories', doc, changedUpdate());
      allow delete: if isAdmin() && hasDeleteAudit('categories', doc);
    }

    match /products/{doc} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create: if isAdminOrManager()
        && request.resource.data.price is int
        && request.resource.data.price > 0
        && productBasePriceOk()
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'products', doc, changedCreate());
      // The products-rule inStock cross-check (productsInStockOk) is
      // DROPPED (contract §3 decision). The second branch is the
      // §13 anonymous/authenticated inStock refresh (verified
      // against inventory, no audit); it is checked first so an
      // audited admin write never pays for it and a refresh never
      // trips over the missing operationId in the admin branch.
      allow update: if productsRefreshOk(doc)
        || (isAdminOrManager()
          && (!('price' in request.resource.data)
            || (request.resource.data.price is int && request.resource.data.price > 0))
          && productBasePriceOk()
          && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'products', doc, changedUpdate()));
      allow delete: if isAdminOrManager() && hasDeleteAudit('products', doc);
    }

    // ---- Orders: created by the client order transaction
    // (storefront anonymous, manual authenticated). Anonymous reads
    // are the idempotency probe only: get of a doc that does not
    // exist yet — an existing order stays unreadable anonymously. ----
    match /orders/{doc} {
      // Price + availability per line live inside orderShapeOk's
      // subtotal sum (Option 1, M1 2026-11-27): the poison-value
      // traversal proves validity AND the subtotal in one walk.
      // Audit-split (M1, approved 2026-11-27): the order rule no
      // longer verifies an audit entry — the audit is written by
      // the client AFTER the order commits (best-effort); "every
      // order has a matching audit entry" is best-effort now, with
      // the admin orphan-order repair as the backstop.
      allow create: if orderShapeOk(doc)
        && orderFeeOk()
        && (request.resource.data.source == 'storefront' || manualOrderAllowed());
      allow get: if isAdminOrManager()
        || (request.auth == null && resource == null);
      allow list: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow update: if isAdminOrManager()
        && orderTransitionOk()
        && (!('status' in request.resource.data)
          || request.resource.data.status in ['new', 'accepted', 'preparing', 'ready', 'in_transit', 'delivered', 'cancelled', 'expired'])
        && (!('paymentStatus' in request.resource.data)
          || request.resource.data.paymentStatus in ['cod_pending', 'cod_paid', 'cod_refused', 'cod_failed'])
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'orders', doc, changedUpdate());
      allow delete: if isAdmin() && hasDeleteAudit('orders', doc);
    }

    // ---- Inventory: admin/manager audited writes, plus the
    // unaudited pure-reservation write of the order transaction
    // (checked first — an authenticated manual-order reservation
    // must not pay the admin branch's inventoryInStockOk getAfter,
    // which would break the per-request budget). Anonymous get
    // (never list): the order transaction reads availability. ----
    match /inventory/{doc} {
      allow get: if isAdminOrManager() || request.auth == null;
      allow list: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if isAdminOrManager()
        && request.resource.data.stock is int && request.resource.data.stock >= 0
        && request.resource.data.reserved is int && request.resource.data.reserved >= 0
        && request.resource.data.reserved <= request.resource.data.stock
        && inventoryInStockOk(doc)
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'inventory', doc, changedCreate());
      allow update: if inventoryReserveOk(doc)
        || (isAdminOrManager()
          && (!('stock' in request.resource.data)
            || (request.resource.data.stock is int && request.resource.data.stock >= 0))
          && (!('reserved' in request.resource.data)
            || (request.resource.data.reserved is int && request.resource.data.reserved >= 0))
          && request.resource.data.reserved <= request.resource.data.stock
          && inventoryInStockOk(doc)
          && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'inventory', doc, changedUpdate()));
      allow delete: if isAdminOrManager() && hasDeleteAudit('inventory', doc);
    }

    // ---- Stock movements: append-only. Admin writes (cancel /
    // deliver / expire) keep the existing admin-only path; the
    // anonymous branch is the exact reserve shape of the order
    // transaction. ----
    match /movements/{doc} {
      allow read: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if isAdminOrManager() || movementReserveOk();
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    // ---- Discount codes: REMOVED 2026-11-27 (Mohamed's decision —
    // the promo code goes entirely). The /discounts collection has
    // no match block any more, so no read/write of any kind is
    // allowed on it; the claim helper and the order-create code
    // check are gone too. Per-product SALE prices (Model P:
    // basePrice/saleSavings) and the delivery fee are untouched.
    // Legacy orders carrying discountCode/discountPercent/
    // discountAmount stay updatable: the three keys remain in the
    // order hasOnly list with no value checks (see orderShapeOk). ----

    // ---- Template registry (Phase 3 v1 + bundle model, 2026-11-27):
    // anonymous get of an ACTIVE registry doc is allowed (the live
    // shell + preview resolution read it); a draft is admin/manager
    // only, never a list. (Widened from the old pointer-scoped read —
    // the old rule allowed anonymous get only of the pointed-to doc;
    // entry 20 requires any active doc to be readable anonymously.)
    // Create/update are admin-only, audited, shape- + status-machine-
    // checked (see the helpers above). A new doc is born 'draft', or
    // 'active' with an approval record — except classic, whose seed
    // is the frozen live site itself. Classic is pinned: its status
    // must stay 'active' and it can never be deleted. Activation
    // history is the subcollection below — append-only, one doc per
    // activation/rollback/retire. Orders carry no templateId (the
    // order shape's hasOnly list is unchanged) and feedback keeps its
    // 5-or-6-field shape (D8) — neither is touched here. ----
    match /templates/{doc} {
      allow get: if isAdminOrManager()
        || (resource != null && resource.data.get('status', null) == 'active');
      allow list: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if isAdmin()
        && templateShapeOk(doc)
        && request.resource.data.get('status', null) in ['draft', 'active']
        && (request.resource.data.get('status', null) == 'draft'
          || doc == 'classic'
          || request.resource.data.get('approval', null) != null)
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'templates', doc, changedCreate());
      allow update: if isAdmin()
        && templateShapeOk(doc)
        && templateStatusTransitionOk(doc)
        && templateFrozenOk()
        && !(doc == 'classic' && request.resource.data.get('status', null) != 'active')
        && (request.resource.data.get('status', null) in ['draft', 'preview', 'retired']
          || request.resource.data.get('approval', null) != null)
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'templates', doc, changedUpdate());
      allow delete: if isAdmin() && doc != 'classic' && hasDeleteAudit('templates', doc);
    }

    // ---- Activation history (spec §2, B5 fix): one doc per
    // activation/rollback/retire, in the templates/{id}/activations
    // subcollection. Append-only — no update, no delete. Admin-only
    // reads (the pointer history stack is the public-facing record;
    // the per-template log is admin detail). ----
    match /templates/{doc}/activations/{operationId} {
      allow get, list: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if isAdmin() && activationShapeOk(doc, operationId);
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    // ---- Preview slugs (Phase 4 B6): ?preview=<slug> resolves
    // through these docs. Anonymous get ONLY, never anonymous list;
    // admin-only create/update (direct writes, no audit entry — the
    // slug document itself is the record); admin list is allowed
    // because rotation queries the open slugs for a template. Admin
    // delete with a delete-audit (revocation is a status write, not
    // a delete). ----
    match /previews/{slug} {
      allow get: if true;
      allow list: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if isAdmin() && previewShapeOk();
      allow update: if isAdmin() && previewShapeOk();
      allow delete: if isAdmin() && hasDeleteAudit('previews', slug);
    }

    match /shippingCompanies/{doc} {
      allow read: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if isAdmin()
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'shippingCompanies', doc, changedCreate());
      allow update: if isAdmin()
        && hasAudit(request.resource.data.get('operationId', null), 'shippingCompanies', doc, changedUpdate());
      allow delete: if isAdmin() && hasDeleteAudit('shippingCompanies', doc);
    }

    // ---- Audit log: append-only, create-only. The admin branch
    // checks actor + operationId == doc id + timestamp; the
    // anonymous branch is the shape-only storefront-order entry
    // (contract §3) — the per-doc rules above check the entry
    // covers their change. ----
    match /audit/{operationId} {
      allow read: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if (isAdminOrManager()
        && request.resource.data.get('actor', null) == request.auth.uid
        && request.resource.data.get('operationId', null) == operationId
        && request.resource.data.get('timestamp', null) == request.time
        && request.resource.data.get('docIds', null) is map
        && request.resource.data.get('docIds', null).size() > 0
        && request.resource.data.get('newValuesByDoc', null) is map)
        || auditAnonOk(operationId);
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    // ---- Rate limits: functions only. No client access at all. ----
    match /rateLimits/{doc} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }

    // ---- Feedback: one-way complaint cards (contract §6). Anonymous
    // create with the exact 5-field shape; admin filing on a
    // customer's behalf writes the same shape. No update (no status
    // / reply any more); admin delete with a delete-audit (spam).
    // The old state machine (feedbackTransitionOk) is gone. ----
    match /feedback/{doc} {
      allow read: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if feedbackOneWayOk();
      allow update: if false;
      allow delete: if isAdmin() && hasDeleteAudit('feedback', doc);
    }

    match /feedback/{doc}/replies/{replyId} {
      allow read: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow update, delete: if false;
    }

    // ---- Spam blocks: functions + admin apps write; nobody reads. ----
    match /feedbackBlocks/{doc} {
      allow read: if false;
      allow create, update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if false;
    }

    // ---- Admin profiles: self-create (bootstrap) + admin manage.
    // A manager reads their own doc (for the permission check). ----
    match /admins/{uid} {
      allow create: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;
      allow get: if request.auth != null && (request.auth.uid == uid || isAdmin());
      allow list: if isAdmin();
      allow update, delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // ---- Phone lookups: get-only by anyone (phone sign-in
    // resolution); listing all lookups is never allowed. ----
    match /phones/{key} {
      allow get: if true;
      allow list: if false;
      allow create: if isAdmin()
        || (request.auth != null && request.resource.data.uid == request.auth.uid);
      allow update, delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // ---- Analytics: shape-checked create + update (pricing §11 /
    // M21 — the attempt-doc shape check); reads and deletes are
    // admin-only. (Decision 19 — the contact stored in attempts —
    // is still open; no change here.) A fabricated doc that fails
    // the shape check is denied. Even so, the rejection-rate signal
    // is indicative-only: the rollout decision must be corroborated
    // by the order-creation rate from rules-checked order docs. ----
    match /analytics/{section}/items/{doc} {
      allow create, update: if attemptShapeOk();
      allow read, delete: if isAdminOrManager();
    }

    // ---- Health: written by the scheduled export + Store Manager
    // health check (admin); read by admins. ----
    match /health/{doc} {
      allow read: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow create, update: if isAdminOrManager();
      allow delete: if false;
    }
  }
}
